  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed change of use within an Economic Use Protection Area without adequate marketing evidence would fail to comply with Policy LP33 of the Local Plan.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal by way of lacking heritage detail and assessment would fail to demonstrate that no harm would be caused to the Grade II* listed Royal Victoria Patriotic Building and Wandsworth Common Conservation Area in contravention of Local Plan (2023) Policy LP3, the London Plan (2021), and the NPPF (2024).",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal would fail to provide adequate provision of cycle storage in contravention of Local Plan (2023) Policy LP51.",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposed units by way of insufficient daylight and outlook and an inadequately sized bedroom would fail to provide a suitable standard of accommodation in contravention of Local Plan (2023) Policy LP27",
    "Reason : 5 - The proposed units would fail to demonstrate adequate waste management and storage in contravention of Local Plan (2023) Policy LP13.",
    "Reason : 6 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to work with the applicant in a positive and proactive manner and the Council has, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan consisting of the Core Strategy, Development Management Policies Document, Supplementary Planning documents and where appropriate the Site Specific Allocations Document as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
